  "analyzer_note": "The three r3a runs packaged a native_stream.py with a rename hook; the committed analyzers apply the same context signal_aliases mapping in their own samples() reader so the frozen native_stream.py of the B cases stays byte-identical.",
  "post_layout_scope": "Extracted SAR macro and extracted CDAC; reference word with cell LPE; comparator and bootstrap schematic; ideal top-level wiring and supplies.",
  "findings": [
    "With the CWORST_T macro, SS cold passes all 8 frames with 6.95 ns of read margin: SAR wiring at worst-case interconnect costs 0.65 ns of the 7.59 ns pre-layout margin, about 13 % of the 5 ns routing reserve.",
    "The typical-RC SS run failed frame 0 because the DC solution left the comparator latch balanced with its clock high (COMP_P/COMP_N 0.42/0.70 V with 256 mV input, unchanged for 60 ns). That start is not physical. Repeated-code stimuli now treat frame 0 as warm-up; in the CWORST_T run the DC start was idle and frame 0 passed anyway.",
    "A sample that aborts a comparison keeps the comparator clock high for 71-72 ps after tracking opens in the pre-layout FF-cold restart runs. No write occurs and tracking overwrites the kickback. single_edge_lpe now reports this overlap as clock_high_at_opening; the restart analyzer does not yet.",
    "The LHCNDQD1 clock latch meets its library minimum pulse widths with large margin at SS cold, FF cold and TT; the tightest is the E high pulse at FF cold, 149 ps against 22 ps."
  ],
  "open_items": [
    "Top-level placement and routing, fill, extraction and the terminal-voltage scan",
    "Report the clock/tracking overlap in the restart analyzer"
  ],
